{"name":"Hexatron","title":"Hexatron","revision":235678,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Hexatron","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hexatron is a vague sci-fi aesthetic that was prominent from the mid-2000s to early 2020s, overlapping with aspects of Frutiger Aero and Flat Design. It is characterized by hexagons, neon blue, holograms, and futuristic technology. It maintains some Frutiger Aero motifs such as futurism, gloss, and 3D graphics, but contrasts it by largely omitting the nature-centered values of Aero, incorporating darker colors, sharp corners, and edges to emphasize abstract technology."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hexatron influences are usually found in modern sci-fi media and real life gaming-tech equipment. It is also adjacent with Cassette Futurism, Cyberpunk, Neo-Vectorheart, and DORFic due to their shared similarities. Though debatably past its time, Hexatron's influences are still seen in modern popular culture."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hexatron has a large focus on sleek and futuristic technology. Common motifs include hexagons, neon blue, holograms, terminal-inspired UIs, and angular technology with heavy ornamentation. It also shares many design elements with Frutiger Aero such as gloss and 3D graphics, but Hexatron largely omits the nature-centered motifs of the latter and leans more into Abstract Tech with its sharp corners and edges."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Half-Life 2 (2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crysis series (2007-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Halo 3 (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Portal (1 & 2) (2007-2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Garry's Mod (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Assassins Creed series (2007-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"WipEout Pulse (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Universe at War: Earth Assault (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Haze (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mirror's Edge (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vanquish (2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tron: Evolution (2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bodycount (2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Binary Domain (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cytus series (2012-2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Phantasy Star Online 2 (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Halo 4 (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Endless Space series (2012-2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Outlast (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Talos Principle series (2014-2023)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Helldivers (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Implosion: Never Lose Hope (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Xenoblade Chronicles X (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rocket League (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Grey Goo (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Civilization: Beyond Earth - Rising Tide (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metroid Prime: Federation Force (2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thumper (2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mirror's Edge Catalyst (2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tron RUN/r (2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Subnautica series (2018-2026)"},{"kind":"list","text":"CrossCode (2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Daemon X Machina series (2019-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Astral Chain (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beat Saber (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metroid Dread (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tron: Identity (2023)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pragmata (2026)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"I, Robot (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Island (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Transformers film series (2007-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"WALL•E (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"TRON: Legacy (2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Prometheus (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ender's Game (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Appleseed Alpha (2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ant-Man (2015)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Alien: Covenant (2017)"},{"kind":"list